# Improve Workbench

This is an explicit, approval-gated utility for improving Workbench itself, not another delivery stage. It has a read-only proposal phase and a separate apply phase.

## Propose

Use evidence from a completed or stopped Workbench run. Inspect the maintained Workbench source and active installed copy when available, but do not edit either. Propose at most one improvement only for a concrete, reusable workflow gap. Prefer no proposal for one-off product decisions, repository-specific facts, transient environment failures, personal data, or behavior already covered by the current skills.

Give the proposal a short identifier and show the evidence, exact intended behavior, source and installed files, overfitting risk, validation, and synchronization plan. State that no Workbench files changed. Delivery-task approval, autopilot authorization, silence, task notes, and suggestions do not approve the proposal.

## Apply an approved proposal

Apply only when the human user directly approves the named proposal or exact displayed change. Re-read the source and installed copy first. If drift changes the patch, stop and show the revised proposal for approval.

Update maintained source before installed copies. Keep the patch narrow and general; preserve authorization boundaries; avoid ticket-specific examples, secrets, memories, and unrelated repository instructions. Update help and host mirrors only when the interface changes. Do not change versions, publish, reinstall, or modify another skill/plugin unless explicitly included in the approved proposal.

Validate changed skills, inspect the final diff, then synchronize and compare active copies byte-for-byte. Report blocked validation or inactive cache honestly. Loaded instructions may require a new session or plugin reload. Do not generate another proposal from this improvement run.
